title: '[revive] test: dry-run max_storage_deposit from an unfunded account'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    ## Summary

    Adds a regression test that verifies a `bare_call` dispatched with the
    runtime-api dry-run `ExecConfig` from an account with no balance still
    reports the same `max_storage_deposit` as a funded run on the same call.

    This is the property wallets / SDKs rely on to size the allowance
    needed to cover the storage deposit before submitting the real
    transaction.

    Each call is wrapped in a rolled-back storage layer so state from the
    reference (funded) run doesn't leak into the unfunded run and skew its
    deposit accounting.

    ## Test plan

    - [x] `SKIP_WASM_BUILD=1 cargo test -p pallet-revive --lib metering::tests::max_storage_deposit_reported_for_unfunded_dry_run`
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
